      "writtenOn": "2016-07-29T17:57:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still don\u0027t really understand this use case for this one. It\u0027s also an anti-pattern to have to drop user IDs into configuration files after keystone has already been deployed. I\u0027d suggest ripping this feature out and proposing it as a discrete patch so that this use case can be discussed in isolation.\n\nRealistically, either people are going to enable this feature because they need to be compliant, or they\u0027re not going to enable it. I can\u0027t imagine anyone will be able to justify a partially PCI compliant deployment as being useful.",
      "revId": "4eff51da89b8300c84b85f400e76a7dd2f5d010e",
